#pragma once

// Zodiacal light at 500 nm outside the atmosphere, in S10 (10th-magnitude stars per square degree),
// from Leinert et al. 1998, "The 1997 reference of diffuse night sky brightness", A&AS 127, 1, Table 17:
// helio-ecliptic longitude from the sun lambda - lambda_sun = 0..180 deg (rows) by ecliptic latitude
// beta = 0..90 deg (columns), both in 5 deg steps. The cells within ~30 deg of the sun, which the
// paper leaves blank, are filled with the brightness extrapolated toward the F corona; they only
// matter in deep twilight, low near the sun's azimuth.

